# Lecture Notes Compiler - Cursor AI Rules

When asked to compile, summarize, or format lecture slides into study notes or PDFs:

1. Target Dimensions:
   - Default: US Legal (8.5in x 14in / 612pt x 1008pt) with 0.18in margin.
   - Alternatives: US Letter (8.5in x 11in) or ISO A4 (210mm x 297mm).
2. Typography and Palette:
   - Body font: Arial 8.0px, line-height 1.13.
   - Strict monochrome / grayscale styling (#000, #fff, #e2e2e2, #f4f4f4).
   - No decorative banners, no slide numbers, and no slide source tags.
3. Anti-Collision Table Rules:
   - Always use table-layout: fixed; width: 100%;.
   - Never exceed 3 or 4 columns within a single column.
   - Always declare explicit percentage colgroup widths.
   - Use word-break: break-word; overflow-wrap: break-word; hyphens: auto; on all td and th cells.
4. Density and Verification:
   - Every page should target 85% to 98% fullness.
   - Run python scripts/verify_pdf.py on compiled output to ensure 0 text collisions.
